Day 42/100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge
Today's challenge focused on mastering Greedy Algorithms through two classic optimization problems.
Problem 1. Leetcode: 1710. Maximum Units on a Truck
Approach:
 Sorted the box types in descending order of units per box. Starting from the box type with the highest units, I greedily loaded as many boxes as possible until the truck was full. This ensures every available slot contributes the maximum possible number of units.

Time Complexity: O(n log n) (Sorting)
 Space Complexity: O(1) (Ignoring sorting space)

Problem 2 Leetcode : 135. Candy
Approach:
 Used a two-pass Greedy approach:
In the first (left-to-right) pass, ensured every child with a higher rating than the left neighbor received more candies.
In the second (right-to-left) pass, ensured the same condition for the right neighbor while preserving the previous assignments using max().
Finally, summed all the candies to obtain the minimum valid distribution.

Time Complexity: O(n)
 Space Complexity: O(n)

Key Takeaways:
1) Learned that sorting by the most beneficial choice first often leads to an optimal greedy solution.
2) Understood how multiple greedy passes can satisfy constraints from different directions.
3) Strengthened my understanding of optimization problems where making locally optimal decisions leads to a globally optimal solution.
